<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ronald Venetiaan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1936</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ronald Venetiaan is a Surinamese mathematician and politician, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-of-suriname">National Party of Suriname</a>, who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> from 1991 to 1996 and again from 2000 to 2010. His first government, elected after military rule, concluded the 1992 peace accord that ended the interior war and introduced economic reforms. He is regarded as a central figure of Suriname's return to democracy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ronald-venetiaan.jpg" alt="Ronald Venetiaan" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wilson Dias/ABr · CC BY 3.0 br · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ronald_Venetiaan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
